(Two lists are equal when they have the same length and equal elements in
 the same places, nested lists and maps included; two maps when they hold
 the same keys with equal values, in any order. A number and a float are
 different elements.)
a list called xs is ["a", 1, 2.5, true, nothing].
a list called ys is ["a", 1, 2.5, true, nothing].
If xs is equal to ys then, print "flat lists equal".
a list called nested is [[1, ["deep"]], {"k": [2]}].
a list called again is [[1, ["deep"]], {"k": [2]}].
If nested is again then, print "nested lists equal".
a list called other is [[1, ["DEEP"]], {"k": [2]}].
If nested is not other then, print "a deep difference is seen".
a list called wholes is [1].
a list called floats is [1.0].
If wholes is not floats then, print "a number is not a float".
a list called shorter is ["a", 1].
If xs is not shorter then, print "different lengths differ".
a list called copied is xs.
If copied is xs then, print "a named copy is equal".
append "z" to copied.
If copied is not xs then, print "after the append they differ".
a list called gone is ["a"].
Free gone.
a list called nothing_left is [].
If gone is nothing_left then, print "a freed list equals an empty one".
a map called stock is {"apples": 3, "pears": [1, 2]}.
a map called order is {"pears": [1, 2], "apples": 3}.
If stock is equal to order then, print "maps equal in any order".
a map called 'apples only' is {"apples": 3}.
If stock is not 'apples only' then, print "a missing key differs".
a map called changed is {"apples": 4, "pears": [1, 2]}.
If stock is not changed then, print "a changed value differs".
a map called snapshot is stock.
If snapshot is stock then, print "a named copy is equal".
